ed space; a marginal Gaussian law alone does not identify E(v). This is a manuscript construction, not a Lean declaration.","citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-gaussian-root-calculus"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"circuit.gaussian_root_calculus","kind":"claim","label":"Root shift and classical Gaussian first chaos","locator":"02-foundations.tex:151–365; eq:root-shift, prop:energy (continuity), subsec:classical-gaussian-sector, eq:classical-first-chaos","source_id":"circuit-r2-26-source-foundations","statement":"On the recursive pointed Fock space, L is an isometry on centered child vectors and vanishes on the vacuum. E(v)=Re⟨v,Lv⟩ and |E(v)−E(w)|≤(‖v‖+‖w‖)‖v−w‖. For real centered directions f, G(f)=q(f) is a commuting Gaussian field, E[G(f)G(g)]=⟨f,g⟩ and ‖G(f)−G(g)‖=‖f−g‖. For orthonormal e_j and an L² function F of their child fields, L*F=Σ_j E[F G(e_j)]e_j.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.gaussian_root_calculus","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.bounded_trigonometric","id":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22circuit.bounded_trigonometric%22%2C%22circuit.gaussian_root_calculus%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22circuit.bounded_trigonometric%22%2C%22circuit.gaussian_root_calculus%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.gaussian_root_calculus"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.classical_strong_limit","id":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22circuit.classical_strong